cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CohortStudio in academic or clinical research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CohortStudio: Clinical cohort data, from raw file to reproducible evidence"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, local-first application for observational cohort studies: data quality, a toggleable
  analysis population with its participant flow, multiple imputation pooled with Rubin's rules, guided
  statistics and survival models, and a Word study dossier that states what every result was computed on.
authors:
  - family-names: "El Mernissi"
    given-names: "Karim"
version: "2.4.1"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23436094"  # the concept DOI: it resolves to the latest version archived on Zenodo
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/KarimELMERNISSI/Cohort-Studio"
url: "https://karimelmernissi.github.io/Cohort-Studio/"
keywords:
  - biostatistics
  - clinical research
  - cohort study
  - epidemiology
  - multiple imputation
  - survival analysis
  - reproducible research
